# Secrets — never commit.
# `.env` alone matches only that exact name, so a `.env.bak` left behind by an
# edit would have been committed with a live refresh token in it. Ignore every
# .env variant and re-include the example explicitly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Token cache (also lives in ~/.alation by default, but just in case)
.token_cache.json

# Deployment state records what we created in a CUSTOMER's catalog, by id.
# Instance-specific and not shareable — but never delete it while a deployment
# is live, or teardown loses track of what it made.
.deployment-state*.json

# Agent name -> UUID map. Instance-specific, for the same reason as the state
# file above: a UUID minted on one tenant means nothing on another.
#
# This was committed until 2026-09-08, and it bit exactly as you would expect.
# Cloning the repo to deploy into a second tenant carried the first tenant's
# UUIDs along with it, and `deploy` checks the lockfile before doing a live
# name match — so it looks up an agent, finds an id that exists nowhere on the
# target, and fails confusingly instead of creating cleanly.
#
# The settled delivery model is a clonable package deployed into a CUSTOMER's
# instance, so every clone shipping the previous tenant's ids was a bug waiting
# for its second user. Keep it local; `deploy` rebuilds it by name match.
.lockfile.json

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Extracted source text and generated output — regenerate, don't commit.
# If you later decide a specific artifact IS a deliverable, un-ignore it
# explicitly with another ! line rather than loosening this rule.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# OS
.DS_Store

# Agent-authored policy specs: regenerable, and NOT reproducible run to
# run (policy_author gave 7 policies once and 6 the next time from identical
# inputs). A committed copy is one sample masquerading as canonical, which is
# how two specs came to share refs with different titles. The measured result
# of each prompt version lives in prompts/policy_author.meta.yaml instead.
policies/*.generated.json

# API response dumps — these carry a real client_id.
*.raw.json
